# Rust / native core (pysuricata-core)
# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this crate ships wheels, so pinning
# the exact dependency versions that built them is what makes a release
# reproducible. (Ignoring it is the convention for library crates, not for
# anything that produces a distributed artifact.)
native/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Build snapshot produced by uv's source-build machinery
_snapshot.tar.gz

# Reports written by documentation examples when the checker executes them.
# check_docs runs every self-contained fence, and several call save_html().
/*_report.html
/report.html
/reports/
/stats.json
/baseline.json
/check.json
/events.parquet
/events.arrow
_snap*.tar.gz

# Generated by scripts/regenerate_example_report.py, which every docs workflow
# runs before `mkdocs build`, so the published site always carries a current
# copy. Committing it too meant every rendering change either produced a
# megabyte diff or drifted silently -- and it drifted, for 45 versions, from
# 0.0.17 until it was 1,180,196 bytes against 600,028 of real output.
# `mkdocs build --strict` does not need it present.
docs/assets/titanic_report.html

# Local scratch. Ignored so a `git add -A` during a conflict resolution cannot
# sweep it into a commit -- which it did once.
_to_delete/
README.draft.md

# Review aid from scripts/contact_sheet.py (#124). Regenerated on demand and
# uploaded by CI as an artifact; never a committed asset.
contact-sheet/
